# ==== T-FMT-B — name-string site 1/8: `format_test`.
# SCOPE CLAIM: this cell samples the `test "…"` NAME-string emit site ONLY,
# across SIX escape costumes in one name: \x41 · \" · \t · \n · \\ · \u{1F600}.
# It says nothing about any other site — each of the other seven has its own
# fixture. Pre-fix RED: the name is re-emitted DECODED (`\x41`->`A`, `\"`->a
# bare quote that breaks the string, `\t`->a literal TAB), so `gg fmt` output
# does not re-parse.
test "esc \x41 quote \" tab \t nl \n back \\ emoji \u{1F600}":
    assert 1 == 1
